      "title": "Simplifying Expressions in Radians Using the Sum and Difference Formulas"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8772da7c-8c3a-5c84-bf5f-6835e30d9690",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\cos\\left(x+\\pi\\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ or $\\cos x$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u+v)=\\cos u\\cos v-\\sin u\\sin v\n$$\n\nWith $u=x$ and $v=\\pi$, the exact values are $\\cos(\\pi)=-1$ and $\\sin(\\pi)=0$. Substitute and collect the terms in the requested order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos\\left(x+\\pi\\right)&=\\cos x\\cos\\left(\\pi\\right)-\\sin x\\sin\\left(\\pi\\right)\\\\\n&=\\cos x\\cdot\\left(-1\\right)-\\sin x\\cdot\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\cos x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0ee67e9a-f950-5aa3-9c32-160af2c8772d",
